            "type": "text/html"
          }
        ]
      },
      "note": [
        "Note that a level of education comprises both studies concluded with a degree and studies concluded without a degree, excluding postgraduate studies that only include persons with degrees. An education must cover no less than one term of full-time studies to enable level classification. \r\n  For further information on principles for classifying the level of education, see www.scb.se/sun",
        "For the 2000 version, the Swedish Register of Education underwent extensive quality improvements which led to a break in the time series and this means that comparisons with previous versions of the register must be done very carefully!     -1) SUN, the Swedish Educational Terminology, was adapted to the international terminology ISCED 97 (International Standard Classification of Education) with the new SUN 2000.    -2) A number of new data sources were added to the register. The most important new sources were:   -*Total higher education points from 1993 from the Higher Education Register*    -*Total KOMVUX (adult education) points from 1988*    -*Foreign educational programmes which are recognised by the National Agency for Higher Education*    -*The National Board of Healths register of healthcare and medical staff*.",
        "XX",
        "Note that educational data might be incomplete for a small number of persons. It could concern people with degrees from abroad or with private degrees or with internal company-educations or people with old degrees."
      ],
